# DSE335 automatic transfer switch controller, GenComm protocol.
# Address = page * 256 + offset. Pages 6 and 7 use the 3xx layout.
# Monitoring map: read-only. Control registers (page 16) are left out on
# purpose; writing them operates the transfer switch.
# Sentinels: 0xFFFF / 0x7FFF (16-bit) and 0xFFFFFFFF / 0x7FFFFFFF (32-bit)
# mean unimplemented; the values just below them mean over range, under
# range, transducer fault, bad data, high or low digital input.
# Checked on a real DSE335 (RS485, 9600 8N2) on 2026-10-13: status, battery,
# S1 voltages and frequency, phase rotation and clock read correctly.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Deep Sea Electronics
@model=DSE335
@description=Automatic transfer switch controller (3xx family), GenComm Modbus protocol. S1 and S2 are the two supplies; Load is the switched output
@source=Deep Sea Electronics, "GenComm standard for use with generating set control equipment" v2.272 (2025-07-21): pages 3, 4, 6 and 7 (3xx register allocation)
@protocol=rtu
@parity=N
@databits=8
@stopbits=2
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@max_read_registers=125
@enum_control_mode=0=Stop|1=Auto|2=Manual|3=Test on load|4=Auto with manual restore|5=User configuration|6=Test off load|7=Off
@enum_phase_rotation=0=Indeterminate|1=L1-L2-L3|2=L3-L2-L1|3=Phase error

name,group,area,address,type,length,scale,offset,unit,access,byte_order,bit,enum,description
